# Phase 7 (Frontend Production Readiness). Keeps the build context sent to
# the Docker daemon small (faster builds) and keeps secrets/dev-only
# artifacts out of any image layer -- COPY . . in infra/docker/web.Dockerfile
# only ever sees what's left after this filter.

# Local env files -- real secrets belong in the deployment platform's
# secret store / Compose env_file:, never baked into an image layer.
# .env.example IS committed (documented defaults) and stays in context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control metadata -- explicitly excluded per docs/architecture/
# 09-infrastructure.md §1 ("do not include ... source-control metadata in
# the final layer").
.git
.gitignore

# Next.js build output + node_modules -- regenerated fresh in the Dockerfile's
# own deps/builder stages; a host-built copy would bake in the host's
# architecture (see api.Dockerfile's identical reasoning for venvs).
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated test-runner artifacts -- never copied into an image.
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# NOTE: `test/`, `e2e/`, vitest.config.ts, and playwright.config.ts are
# deliberately NOT excluded. `next build` typechecks every .ts/.tsx the
# tsconfig `include` globs (tsconfig.json: `**/*.ts`, `**/*.tsx`), and the
# app's own `__tests__/` files import `@/test/*` (path alias `@/*` ->
# `./*`, tsconfig.json) -- dropping `test/` here made the container's
# typecheck diverge from the host's and fail the build (TS2307). Keeping
# these small source dirs in the context keeps the container's typecheck
# identical to the host's. They're only a few KB of fixtures/handlers.

# Debug/log files.
*.log
*.pem

# Editor/OS cruft.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# This directory itself -- Dockerfiles never need to COPY themselves.
infra/docker/
